          "title": "A Visit in the Rain",
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "text": "Jacob lived in a small house near the coast. He loved the sea, but he also loved his old books. One day, Jacob decided to visit a friend who lived in a large villa on the hill. The villa had been restored, so it looked new and clean, without any dust on the walls. Jacob wanted to bring a gift, but he did not have any money for a new book. He decided to borrow a rare book from the local library, promising to give it back in a week."
            },
            {
              "text": "As he left his house, the sky turned grey. A few moments later, it started to rain. Jacob did not have an umbrella to keep himself dry, so he had to use his coat to cover his head. The rain was heavy, and he got wet. He walked slowly, thinking about the risks of walking in a storm. He did not want the borrowed book to get wet, so he held it tight against his chest."
            },
            {
              "text": "When he finally arrived at the villa, his friend Victor welcomed him. Victor was a distinguished man who spent his time studying history. They sat in the living room and talked about many things. Victor liked the book Jacob had brought and suggested they read it together. They spent the whole afternoon in the quiet room, enjoying the story and the sound of the rain outside. Jacob was happy that he chose to visit his friend despite the bad weather."
            }
          ]
        },
