          "title": "Fixing the Greenhouse",
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "text": "Tom loved his garden, but his small greenhouse needed work. The warm building where he grew food had a broken pane, a single piece of glass that had cracked during the winter. He called his friend, Sam, to help him fix it."
            },
            {
              "text": "Sam arrived with a heavy bag of tools. He did not have a machine to make holes, so he had to borrow one from the neighbor. After getting the tool, the two friends started to work. They carefully removed the old glass and cleaned the metal frame."
            },
            {
              "text": "Tom used a hammer to hit the nails into the wood, making sure the new glass was tight. They worked quickly in the quiet morning air. By noon, the greenhouse was sturdy again, strong enough to stand against the wind. The two friends sat down to rest, feeling proud of their hard work."
            }
          ]
        },
